            "review_text": "Simon P\n112 contributions\n0\nGreat place for lunch near the War Museum\nAug 2014 • Couples\nWe picked this place at random during lunch break at the War Museum. Level one is open to the air, level two is sealed with air con. We had a couple of varieties of rice paper rolls which were very good. The signature dish seems to be curry with baguette, or roll-ups of various things in lettuce. The locals eating there were very enthusiastic about their lunch, so we went in and it was very good.\nRead more\nWritten August 31, 2014",
